  "description": "NOCBUD crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H78 Br8 Eu5 F12 N8 O34 S4 1+,C1 F3 O3 S1 1-,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2B (Eu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.636-4.037 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.36-113.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu5L4(CF3SO3)4(MeO)2(H2O)4]·CF3SO3·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
